# Virtualenvs and caches
.venv/
__pycache__/
*.py[cod]
.pytest_cache/
.hypothesis/
.coverage
.mypy_cache/
.ruff_cache/

# Build output. Regenerated by each project's own build script; the toolchain
# versions that matter are pinned in 02-*/toolchain/versions.lock and recorded
# in 09-*/contracts/contracts.lock.yaml.
build/
*/build/
cmake-build-*/
*.o
*.a
*.so

# Run artifacts and generated evidence. These are the OUTPUT of a run, not its
# definition: 09-*/compose/pipeline/run-pipeline.sh plus the lock reproduce
# them. Keeping them would add ~110 MB of data that is stale the moment the
# code changes.
runs/
*/runs/
*/reports/runs/
*/.artifacts/
out/
#
# P09's reports/ is output in its entirety, so it is named rather than matched.
# The first commit tracked audit.json, infra.json, infra-observed.json,
# pipeline.log and persistence.log, all written by runs on one laptop: they
# carry that host's paths, its Kafka cluster id and the timestamps of those
# runs. A committed audit.json is worse than no audit.json, because it reads as
# this checkout's verdict when it is a snapshot of someone else's machine. CI
# writes its own and uploads it as a build artifact
# (.github/workflows/p09-contracts.yml); nothing reads a committed copy.
#
# A blanket */reports/ was the first attempt and was wrong: P02's reports/
# holds interop.json and cpp-cases.json, which are conformance baselines a
# reviewer is meant to diff, and P08 keeps a report template there. Those
# projects ignore their own run output themselves -- P03 and P07 each track
# only a reports/.gitkeep -- so the only directory this file needs to speak
# for is P09's.
09-full-system-integration/reports/

# Generated C++ proto code. Regenerated from the canonical schema by
# 02-*/scripts/generate_proto.sh, and the schema itself is guarded by
# `p09 sync-schema --check`, which is what actually needs reviewing.
*/cpp/generated/

# P05's generated *_pb2.py is deliberately NOT ignored. It looks like a build
# artifact and is not one: P05 pins [contracts].protobuf_descriptor_sha256
# against the descriptor compiled into that file, so regenerating it with a
# different protobuf version moves the pin. The generated code is part of the
# contract, and P05's own .gitignore leaves it versioned for the same reason.

# Local editor state
.vscode/
.idea/

# Nothing in this repository should ever hold a credential. These patterns are
# a backstop, not a policy: the policy is 09-*/README.md (NFR-09) and the
# secret-scan step in .github/workflows/p09-contracts.yml.
*.pem
*.key
.env
.env.*
!.env.example
